    "title": "BILLS GAME WEEK: Buffalo returns home to host Cincinnati Sunday (preview) - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kyle Evans ,\n31 minutes ago The Buffalo Bills return to Highmark Stadium on Sunday for a Week 14 matchup against the Cincinnati Bengals, with kickoff set for 1 p.m.\nBuffalo sits at 8-4 after a dominant road win over the Pittsburgh Steelers, while Cincinnati enters at 4-8 but coming off a convincing 32-14 victory over the Baltimore Ravens in Joe Burrow’s return.\nThe Bills lead the NFL in rushing at 155.7 yards per game and just produced 249 yards on the ground in Pittsburgh, yet this matchup presents an opportunity for balance against a Bengals defense ranked near the bottom against both the pass and the run.\nBuffalo has been one of the NFL’s best December teams under Sean McDermott, going 18-3 in the month since 2020 while averaging more than 30 points per game and allowing fewer than 20.\nThis will be the 35th meeting between the Bills and Bengals. The series is tied 17-17, though Cincinnati has won the last two games, including their 2022 postseason matchup.\nGAME WEEK LINKS PRESS CONFERENCES\nFROM SOCIAL MEDIA",
